| Task | Open |
|---|---|
| Config files & sections | `references/presets/conf.md` |
| HTTP server / routes | `references/presets/http.md` |
| Typed API + frontend codegen | `references/presets/api.md` |
| Toolbox binary: subcommands, `--json`, doctor | `references/presets/cli.md` |
| Auth: strategies, sessions, keys, OIDC/JWT | `references/presets/auth.md` |
| Tracing / OpenTelemetry | `references/presets/otel.md` |
| Registration, params, scopes, lifecycle, testing | `references/kernel.md` |
| Hit an error code | `references/errors.md` or `ultra explain <code>` |
| Inspect the graph / drift | `references/graph.md` |

Growing past what is wired (pg, migrate, authpg, redis, ws, s3, inference)? Each
is one registration — read that preset's reference in the ultrastack module.

## Commands (the binary is a toolbox)

```
go run .                    # serve (opens the admin socket too)
go run . routes | health    # auth table / live causal health
go run . graph | blast      # graph summary / blast radius
go run . doctor --json      # support bundle for tickets
go run . config reference   # annotated config docs
go run . openapi            # OpenAPI 3.1 contract
go run . client --out src/lib/api   # typed Svelte client (TanStack hooks)
```

## Testing layers

1. unit: hand-construct (di.Many literals, di.Some/None, di.LazyOf,
   di.ScopeFunc, di.FamilyFixed, di.SyncRunner) — never the container.
2. wiring: `TestWiring` (stack.Validate) — the covenant.
3. integration: `di.TestApp(t, di.Options(Modules()...), di.Swap[X](fake))`.
